th: the per-effect recheck refuses the same verdict, but only the entry arm leaves the key unbound, so the killer's no-bind assertion reddens.\",\n952|    ),\n953|    Mutant(\n954|        name=\"N-lifecycle-loop-generation\",\n955|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/ops.go\",\n956|        find='\\t\\tif lc.CurrentGeneration() != mctx.BackendGeneration {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn fail(terminalbackend.CodeStaleGeneration, \"backend_generation stale\")\\n\\t\\t}\\n',\n957|        replace='\\t\\tif lc.CurrentGeneration() != mctx.BackendGeneration && lc.CurrentGeneration() != \"generation-two\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn fail(terminalbackend.CodeStaleGeneration, \"backend_generation stale\")\\n\\t\\t}\\n',\n958|        count=1,\n959|        run=\"TestExecuteRestoreRefusesGenerationDrift\",\n960|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n961|        note=\"Admits exactly generation-two past the per-effect generation recheck; every other stale generation still refuses. Kill path: the drifted restore executes under the stale binding instead of refusing.\",\n962|    ),\n963|    Mutant(\n964|        name=\"N-lifecycle-restore-authkind\",\n965|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/ops.go\",\n966|        find='deadline, terminstance.AuthorizationRestore, reqBackend, func(result terminstance.Result) OpOutcome {',\n967|        replace='deadline, terminstance.AuthorizationControl, reqBackend, func(result terminstance.Result) OpOutcome {',\n968|        count=1,\n969|        run=\"TestExecuteRestore\",\n970|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n971|        note=\"Rewires exactly the restore effect loop to the control authorization kind; the entry check still demands restore. Kill path: the kind mismatch refuses at the first effect recheck instead of restoring.\",\n972|    ),\n973|    Mutant(\n974|        name=\"N-lifecycle-terminate-authkind\",\n975|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/ops.go\",\n976|        find='deadline, terminstance.AuthorizationForceStale, reqBackend, func(result terminstance.Result) OpOutcome {',\n977|        replace='deadline, ter