te-record write, B34 discloses reopening, README narrowed | B43 text in TRACEABILITY + matrix; no fourth guard added |\n23|| P1-B | in-flight attach commits after successful quiescence (logical check/use race, no data race) | FIXED — one ordering contract at the effect boundary: attach rechecks the barrier under `barrierMu` immediately before its receipt commit and holds it through receipt, returned vector, and memory; quiesce holds it across engine closure plus report, boundary across its report only | `TestAttachRefusesAfterQuiescenceWhenAdmittedLate`, `TestAttachQuiesceOrderingOverlapQuiesce`, `TestAttachQuiesceOrderingOverlapBoundary` via `Lifecycle.Execute`; narrowings `N-attach-barrier-recheck`, `N-ordering-lock-{attach,quiesce,boundary}` |\n24|| P2-A | three read-error narrowings survive (incarnation EISDIR, outcomes ENOTDIR, outcome-file EISDIR) | FIXED — three production-entry tests plus three reviewer-shaped narrowings; attach custody entry carries its own valid-body test plus narrowing | tests + `N-incarnation-read-absent`, `N-outcomes-dir-read-absent`, `N-outcome-file-read-skip`, `N-attach-entry-root-custody` |\n25|| P2-B | corpus excludes cloneproject, sshtransport, crashgate on a false premise | FIXED — five representative rows added; corpus covers 36/36 with no exclusion bounds | closure grid 198 shared keys, 0 moved; verdict grid 23,874 shared, 0 moved |\n26|| P3 | Table C denominator stale (129 vs 137 gates); attach \"lease members\" prose; README/row-79 overclaims | FIXED — Table C recounted from the Table D gate set (140 gates incl. 3 new); row 72 corrected; README + row 79 narrowed | recount script over both tables; mirror check TRACEABILITY vs matrix |\n27|\n28|## P1-A — escalation with the boundary (no fourth guard)\n29|\n30|Three boundaries in three rounds is structural: the barrier is\n31|reconstructed from whichever storage artefact survived, so the\n32|failure to create the outcome proof reads as permission. This\n33|revision does not add another guard. Bound B43 (in TRACEABILITY\n34|and mirrored in the matrix) states:\n35|\n36|- Owner: `internal/terminstance ReceiptStore` (landed receipt\n37|  owner). Scoped contract: completed-closure enumeration — the\n38|  completed quiesce/boundary receipts for one instance,\n39|  distinguishing pending-without-completion from completed — so\n40|  attach admission can consult receipt completion as the\n41|  authoritative proof with pending-versus-committed\n42|  representable. This leaf owns the admission side once it\n43|  lands.\n44|- Boundary: a lost outcome-report write after committed closure\n45|  admits a fresh writable attach until the identical retry heals\n46|  the report; the same window covers a crash between the receipt\n47|  commit and the report, and a simultaneous loss of both the\n48|  report and the state record. Retrying the identical quiesce\n49|  heals the report and re-closes input; no other production\n50|  entry heals it.\n51|\n52|Every P1-A-adjacent claim now matches the boundary: row 79\n53|claims only the lost state-record write fails closed (still\n54|proven by `TestExecuteQuiesceStateWriteFailureRefusesWiredAttach`\n55|through the wired attach); B34 discloses reopening before retry;\n56|the README refuses new writable attaches only once the closure\n57|report commits. The rev5 construction (incarnation-scoped proof,\n58|advisory-memory split, writer/reader censuses) stands unchanged\n59|around the bound: the rev4 regressions\n60|(`TestReviewExistingActiveMemoryCannotReopenQuiescedInput`,\n61|`TestReviewFailedStopCannotEraseQuiescence`) and the legitimate\n62|reopening (`TestExecuteQuiesceStopRestoreReopensBarrier`) all\n63|still pass.\n64|\n65|## P1-B — one ordering contract at the effect boundary\n66|\n67|`Lifecycle.barrierMu` serializes the input-closure ordering\n68|contract: the quiesce report commit, the boundary report commit,\n69|and the attach writable-receipt commit (barrier recheck, client\n70|receipt, returned vector, advisory memory) are mutually\n71|exclusive, so whichever lands first wins and no writable receipt\n72|commits after a durable closure report.\n73|\n74|- Attach side (`ops.go:executeAttach`): the fast-path check and\n75|  the server admission run outside the lock (admission may\n76|  block); the authoritative recheck runs under the lock\n77|  immediately before the receipt commit, and the lock holds\n78|  through the receipt, the returned vector, and the memory\n79|  record. The check did not merely move: without the lock the\n80|  overlap tests observe the attach completing mid-commit.\n81|- Quiesce side (`lifecycle.go:executeEngineOp`): the lock spans\n82|  the engine input closure and the report commit, so no receipt\n83|  commits between the tmux closure effects and their durable\n84|  proof. Its tmux effects return immediately, so the span never\n85|  blocks on a signal.\n86|- Boundary side: the wait runs outside the lock (it blocks on\n87|  the wrapper signal); only the report commit serializes.\n88|\n89|The covered vector handoff ends at vector construction: a\n90|caller that execs a pre-quiescence vector after quiescence\n91|commits holds a pre-quiescence authorization, which quiesce does\n92|not revoke (stated on the field and in B42). Cross-process\n93|attach/quiesce races observe only the report files (bound B42:\n94|closing needs a lock file; no committed test stages two\n95|processes).\n96|\n97|Narrowings (all instance-scoped, all KILLED):\n98|`N-attach-barrier-recheck` (recheck bypassed for the fixture\n99|instance — the late attach succeeds),\n100|`N-ordering-lock-attach`, `N-ordering-lock-quiesce`,\n101|`N-ordering-lock-boundary` (one side unlocked for the fixture\n102|instance — the attach completes mid-commit). Symmetry: attach\n103|1 / quiesce 1 / boundary 1. The late-attach and both overlap\n104|tests pass twice under `-race` with no data-race diagnostic.\n105|\n106|## P2-A — the three read-error clauses, witnessed\n107|\n108|| Gap | Committed test (production entry) | Harness row (reviewer plant shape) |\n109||---|---|---|\n110|| R1 incarnation EISDIR as absence | `TestExecuteAttachErrorsOnIncarnationReadFailure` via `Execute(attach)` (incarnation path staged as a directory) | `N-incarnation-read-absent` — admits exactly EISDIR past the absent arm |\n111|| R2 outcomes ENOTDIR as absence | `TestExecuteAttachErrorsOnOutcomesDirReadFailure` via `Execute(attach)` (outcomes path staged as a file) | `N-outcomes-dir-read-absent` — admits exactly ENOTDIR past the absent arm |\n112|| R3 outcome-file EISDIR skipped | `TestExecuteAttachErrorsOnOutcomeFileReadFailure` via `Execute(attach)` (`.json` symlink to a directory, kept by the entry pre-filter) | `N-outcome-file-read-skip` — admits exactly `deadbeef.json` past the error arm |\n113|\n114|Each test asserts the production read-failure string and zero\n115|tmux execs; each plant makes the attach succeed. The attach\n116|custody entry now carries its own valid-body test\n117|(`TestExecuteAttachRefusesWritableRootValidBody`) plus\n118|`N-attach-entry-root-custody` (reviewer R4 shape: custody\n119|bypassed only for attach — the weakened attach is served,\n120|proving admission rather than rerouting to a body refusal).\n121|\n122|## P2-B — importer outcome corpus, 36 of 36\n123|\n124|The fixed-corpus driver (ships in the evidence tarball) gains\n125|five rows and loses all three exclusion bounds:\n126|\n127|- `cloneproject.Normalize` no-fetcher and no-sink refusals\n128|  (deterministic pre-effect arms);\n129|- `sshtransport.New(config.Snapshot{})` invalid-snapshot\n130|  refusal (no SSH, no network);\n131|- `crashgate.Lookup` known (`CR-LAUNCH-D-01`) and unknown\n132|  boundary rows.\n133|\n134|Outcome grid over the reviewer's 36-package closure (34\n135|production + crashgate + environ): 198 shared\n136|`(package, entry, input)` keys, MOVED 0, base-only 0,\n137|candidate-only 7 (the declared `CheckSocketLength` × 2 and\n138|`ClassifyStatus` × 5 story-added entries). Stability: 6/6\n139|identical candidate runs (sha256 match). Suite verdicts over\n140|the complete importer set: 23,874 shared `(package, test)`\n141|keys, zero moved verdicts, zero base-only, 505 candidate-only\n142|additions (500 tmuxserver incl. subtests, 5 termbind), all\n143|PASS, 0 FAILs. No input moved across any admission or refusal\n144|arm: the outcome grid names every probed input and every one\n145|is identical or declared.\n146|\n147|## P3 — census denominator and prose, item by item\n148|\n149|- Table C derives its gate set from Table D: 140 gates × 11 =\n150|  1540 cells (1522 U2a + 18 U2c), adding the 8 revision-5 gates\n151|  the verdict named plus the 3 revision-6 gates (recheck,\n152|  ordering, barrierread). Total census: 255 measured of 5248\n153|  (50+10+195 M; 186 bound; 4807 unreachable), recount verified\n154|  by script over TRACEABILITY and over the matrix.\n155|- Revision-6 Table D: 140 rows × 21 = 2940 (195 M, 182 B, 2563\n156|  U). New rows recheck (EXA 1), ordering (EXA 1 / EXE 2),\n157|  barrierread (EXA 2 arms); incarnationlookup EXA moves B39 →\n158|  measured; rootwrite EXA gains the attach entry row. Every\n159|  two-sided gate carries its symmetry line (ordering attach 1 /\n160|  quiesce 1 / boundary 1; barrierread directory 1 / file 1;\n161|  incarnationlookup EXA 1 / LOOK 3 on different arms; rootwrite\n162|  CUS 1 / EXC 1 / EXA 1 / EXS 1 / EXR 1 / SPW 1 + shared row).\n163|- Row 72 corrected: the attach authorization is\n164|  ownership-neutral with no lease member (identity, client,\n165|  transport, input flag, deadline listed literally).\n166|- Row 79, B34, and the README narrowed to the B43 boundary as\n167|  listed above; battery counts updated (281 tmuxserver rows:\n168|  277 narrowing + 3 supplementary + control; 321/321 across\n169|  both harnesses).\n170|\n171|## Census and ratios\n172|\n173|- Gate × entry census: 255 measured of 5248 (50+10+195 M\n174|  across Tables A/B/D; Table C all U); 186 bound; 4807\n175|  unreachable with reasons; 155 named undriven gaps (147 B39 +\n176|  8 named cells; B40/B41/B42/B43 are non-cell bounds). Tables\n177|  B/D and bounds B22-B43 are byte-identical between\n178|  TRACEABILITY and the conformance matrix (mirror check in the\n179|  evidence).\n180|- AC rows 59-92: 34 of 34 driven through production entries by\n181|  named tests (call sites in the matrix).\n182|- Eight operations, 8 of 8, each through `Lifecycle.Execute`\n183|  (`lifecycle.go`) by a named committed test: create\n184|  (`TestExecuteCreateInteractive`), attach (`TestExecuteAttach`),\n185|  status (`TestExecuteStatusPresent`), quiesce\n186|  (`TestExecuteQuiesce`), safe-boundary (`TestExecuteBoundary`),\n187|  stop (`TestExecuteStop`), stale termination\n188|  (`TestExecuteTerminate`), restore (`TestExecuteRestore`).\n189|- Mutant battery: 281/281 tmuxserver rows as expected (277\n190|  narrowing `N-*` KILLED + 3 additive `D-*` KILLED, shared\n191|  control SURVIVED), 40/40 termbind rows as expected; one raw\n192|  log per plant in the tarball. 8 new tmuxserver rows this\n193|  round, all narrowing.\n194|- No-real-tmux: zero real-tmux witnesses by the determinism\n195|  design (bound B1); the suite passes with the tmux binary\n196|  unresolvable (1000 passing test events, zero failures, zero\n197|  skips in the changed packages; no tmux process before, during,\n198|  or after).\n199|- Handovers retained: exec/probe adapters driven (unchanged);\n200|  B18 sun_path, B16 ambient, B19/B20 custody, and the P3-A\n201|  fresh-decoy attestation witnesses all still pass; this leaf\n202|  extends the landed termbind owner for successor minting and\n203|  composes terminalbackend, terminstance, axpane, and fencing\n204|  without forking (no landed production file touched this\n205|  round).\n206|\n207|## Validation (all exit 0, this run)\n208|\n209|| Gate | Result |\n210||---|---|\n211|| `go test ./... -count=1` candidate / base | 45 ok / 45 ok |\n212|| `go test -race` tmuxserver + termbind | ok, no races |\n213|| `go test ./... -cover` | ok (tmuxserver 88.3%, termbind 83.5%) |\n214|| `go vet ./...` + `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` | clean |\n215|| `gofmt -l` | clean |\n216|| tmuxserver harness 281 + termbind harness 40 | all as expected |\n217|| no-tmux PATH run (changed packages) | green, zero skips |\n218|| closure grid determinism | 6/6 identical streams |\n219|| census recount + matrix mirror check | counts match; tables/bounds byte-identical |\n220|| full configured suite (30 commands) | green firsthand |\n221|\n222|## Evidence\n223|\n224|- `TASK-260830-1c28dz_conformance-matrix.md` (updated, attached):\n225|  AC rows, ops table, mirrored census Tables B/C/D + Table E,\n226|  bounds B22-B43, battery, crash/idempotency.\n227|- `TASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-evidence-rev6.tar.gz` (attached):\n228|  closure grid driver + base/candidate streams + diff,\n229|  per-test verdict streams + diff, full suite logs both trees,\n230|  281 + 40 raw per-plant harness logs, vet/fmt/race/cover/\n231|  no-tmux logs, census recount, mirror check, SHA256SUMS.\n232|- Handoff: ready for review; candidate UNCOMMITTED in the\n233|  Story worktree for snapshot.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
