{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca9b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c8e2-bf86-7413-8196-b3968750220e"},"sequence":936,"recorded_at":1780531400001867,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b7feb475-a410-4d2f-87a4-514d078fdaaf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b7feb475-a410-4d2f-87a4-514d078fdaaf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b7feb475-a410-4d2f-87a4-514d078fdaaf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c8e7-8cbb-7160-9998-37afc1cac5fe"},"task_id":"01a0c8e7-8cbb-7160-9998-37afc1cac5fe","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c8e7-8cbb-7160-9998-37afc1cac5fe","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 109-120\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-\t// Ordering contract, attach side: the fast-path barrier check\n-\t// above ran before the (possibly blocking) server admission,\n-\t// so quiescence may have committed since. Revalidate the\n-\t// barrier under the lock immediately before the receipt\n-\t// commit, and hold the lock through the receipt, the returned\n-\t// vector, and the advisory memory record, so no writable\n-\t// receipt commits after a durable closure report.\n-\tlc.barrierMu.Lock()\n-\tdefer lc.barrierMu.Unlock()\n-\tif err := lc.checkAttachQuiesced(body.TerminalInstanceID, body.InputAuthorized); err != nil {\n-\t\treturn empty, err\n-\t}\n+\t// Ordering contract, attach side: the checks above ran before\n+\t// the (possibly blocking) server admission and the barrier\n+\t// lock wait, so every live fact they observed may have gone\n+\t// stale. The effect boundary below re-observes every live\n+\t// authorization fact under the lock immediately before the\n+\t// receipt commit, and the lock holds through the receipt, the\n+\t// returned vector, and the advisory memory record. The\n+\t// enumeration, first-observed site to revalidation site:\n+\t// closure (fast path above, rechecked here); server\n+\t// generation (admission above, live CurrentGeneration here);\n+\t// request deadline (entry above, live clock here — the lock\n+\t// wait counts against the deadline, and the deadline stays\n+\t// distinct from the authorization expiry); authorization\n+\t// expiry, transport binding, and input binding (entry\n+\t// CheckAttachRequest above, live clock rechecked inside the\n+\t// commit call itself, which holds no wait between its check\n+\t// and its no-replace install, plus the post-commit result\n+\t// binding for input). Transition, operation capability, and\n+\t// backend identity are pure checks over request-immutable\n+\t// members — no live fact, nothing to revalidate. The\n+\t// attestation value is immutable once returned; its live\n+\t// counterpart is the generation rechecked here. Residual: a\n+\t// generation rotation landing between this recheck and the\n+\t// commit (no waits inside, file I/O only) is the inherent\n+\t// check-then-act remainder the cross-process bound B42 owns.\n+\tlc.barrierMu.Lock()\n+\tdefer lc.barrierMu.Unlock()\n+\tif err := lc.checkAttachQuiesced(body.TerminalInstanceID, body.InputAuthorized); err != nil {\n+\t\treturn empty, err\n+\t}\n+\tif !lc.Now().Before(deadline) {\n+\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeTimeout, Detail: \"operation deadline\"}\n+\t}\n+\tif lc.CurrentGeneration() != body.BackendGeneration {\n+\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeStaleGeneration, Detail: \"backend_generation stale\"}\n+\t}\n","final_result":true}}}
