s force_stale. Kill path: the kind mismatch refuses at the first effect recheck instead of killing.\",\n-    ),\n+    Mutant(\n+        name=\"D-lifecycle-restore-authkind\",\n+        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/ops.go\",\n+        find='deadline, terminstance.AuthorizationRestore, reqBackend, func(result terminstance.Result) OpOutcome {',\n+        replace='deadline, terminstance.AuthorizationControl, reqBackend, func(result terminstance.Result) OpOutcome {',\n+        count=1,\n+        run=\"TestExecuteRestore\",\n+        expect=\"KILLED\",\n+        note=\"SUPPLEMENTARY POSITIVE-PATH WIRING, not a narrowing: rewires exactly the restore effect loop to the control authorization kind while the entry still demands restore, so the successful restore refuses at the first effect recheck. It proves the loop consults the passed kind; it admits no forbidden grant. Kill path: the restore receives terminal_backend_unauthorized instead of restoring.\",\n+    ),\n+    Mutant(\n+        name=\"D-lifecycle-terminate-authkind\",\n+        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/ops.go\",\n+        find='deadline, terminstance.AuthorizationForceStale, reqBackend, func(result terminstance.Result) OpOutcome {',\n+        replace='deadline, terminstance.AuthorizationControl, reqBackend, func(result terminstance.Result) OpOutcome {',\n+        count=1,\n+        run=\"TestExecuteTerminate\",\n+        expect=\"KILLED\",\n+        note=\"SUPPLEMENTARY POSITIVE-PATH WIRING, not a narrowing: rewires exactly the terminate effect loop to the control authorization kind while the entry still demands force_stale, so the successful terminate refuses at the first effect recheck. It proves the loop consults the passed kind; it admits no forbidden grant. Kill path: the terminate receives terminal_backend_unauthorized instead of killing.\",\n+    ),\n+    Mutant(\n+        name=\"N-lifecycle-loop-authorization\",\n+        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/ops.go\",\n+        find='\\t\\tif err := terminstance.CheckAuthorization(mctx.Authorization, kind, lc.CurrentLease(), lc.Now()); err != nil {\\n',\n+        replace='\\t\\tif err := terminstance.CheckAuthorization(mctx.Authorization, kind, lc.CurrentLease(), lc.Now()); err != nil && committed {\\n',\n+        count=1,\n+        run=\"TestExecuteTerminateRefusesAuthorizationExpiredAfterReceipt\",\n+        expect=\"KILLED\",\n+        note=\"Admits exactly pre-commit authorization failures past the per-effect recheck (the first effect runs under the lapsed grant); post-commit failures still refuse. Kill path: the expired-after-receipt terminate execs the kill instead of refusing before any effect.\",\n+    ),\n","final_result":true}}}
