hkind EXT 2 / EXR 2 (entry 1 / shared loop 1 each; D-loop wiring\\\\nsupplementary, uncounted); generation EXA 1 / EXT 1 / EXR 2; deadline\\\\nEXA 2 / EXT 1 / EXR 2;\\\", 1)\\n\\n# --- counts ---\\nrep(\\\"140 × 21 = 2940 cells; 195 M, 182\\\", \\\"140 × 21 = 2940 cells; 196 M, 182\\\", 1)\\nrep(\\\"B, 2563 U; counts verified by script over the table)\\\", \\\"B, 2562 U; counts verified by script over the table)\\\", 1)\\nrep(\\\"Ratio: 255 measured of 5248 (50+10+195 M across Tables A/B/D;\\\\nTable C all U); 186 bound; 4807 unreachable\\\",\\n    \\\"Ratio: 256 measured of 5248 (50+10+196 M across Tables A/B/D;\\\\nTable C all U); 186 bound; 4806 unreachable\\\", 1)\\n\\n# --- B42 ---\\nrep(\\\"pre-quiescence authorization, which quiesce does not revoke.\\\\n- B43\\\",\\n    \\\"pre-quiescence authorization, which quiesce does not revoke.\\\\n  The same in-process scope covers the attach post-lock\\\\n  generation and deadline rechecks: a rotation landing between\\\\n  the recheck and the commit \\\\u2014 inside one process or across\\\\n  processes \\\\u2014 is not excluded; the window holds no waits.\\\\n- B43\\\", 1)\\n\\n# --- revision paragraph ---\\nrep(\\\"stated as B43 (receipt-owner enumeration contract), and states B42\\\\n(in-process ordering).\\\",\\n    \\\"stated as B43 (receipt-owner enumeration contract), and states B42\\\\n(in-process ordering). Revision 7 closes the attach\\\\nadmission-to-effect interval for every remaining live fact (the\\\\npost-lock generation and deadline rechecks with the full fact\\\\nenumeration; the authorization facts revalidate inside the\\\\ncommit), moves the generation EXA cell from U1 to measured,\\\\nextends the deadline and authkind cells with the new rows,\\\\nreclassifies the two effect-loop authkind wirings as\\\\nsupplementary D rows beside the genuine shared loop narrowing\\\\nN-lifecycle-loop-authorization, converts the entry authkind rows\\\\nto genuine no-bind narrowings, and extends B42 to the new\\\\nrechecks.\\\", 1)\\n\\n# --- battery ---\\nrep(\\\"internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py`: 281/281 rows as\\\\nexpected (280 KILLED \\\\u2014 277 narrowing `N-*` plus 3 additive\\\\n`D-*` \\\\u2014 and the shared harmless control SURVIVED), run in\\\\nfour chunks across isolated tree copies with one raw log per\\\\nplant in the evidence tarball. The second leaf owns 204\\\\nnarrowing rows.\\\",\\n    \\\"internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py`: 285/285 rows as\\\\nexpected (284 KILLED \\\\u2014 279 narrowing `N-*` plus 5 supplementary\\\\n`D-*` (3 additive + 2 positive-path wiring) \\\\u2014 and the shared\\\\nharmless control SURVIVED), run in\\\\nfour chunks across isolated tree copies with one raw log per\\\\nplant in the evidence tarball. The second leaf owns 208\\\\nnarrowing rows.\\\", 1)\\nrep(\\\"321/321 mutant rows as expected across both harnesses with one\\\\nraw log per plant.\\\",\\n    \\\"325/325 mutant rows as expected across both harnesses with one\\\\nraw log per plant.\\\", 1)\\n\\np.write_text(s)\\nprint(\\\"matrix updated OK\\\")\\nEOF\",\n  \"description\": \"Apply mirrored matrix edits, corrected counts\",\n  \"exit_code\": 1,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"failed\",\n  \"terminal_reason\": \"process exited with status 1\",\n  \"output\": \"Traceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"<stdin>\\\", line 20, in <module>\\n  File \\\"<stdin>\\\", line 8, in rep\\nAssertionError: want 2, found 3: 'TestExecuteTerminateRefusesProviderOnlyCapability, TestExecuteTerminateRefusesOnDeadline, '\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 233,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 59,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
