{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d923","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c8e2-bf86-7413-8196-b3968750220e"},"sequence":2796,"recorded_at":1780531400005587,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b7feb475-a410-4d2f-87a4-514d078fdaaf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b7feb475-a410-4d2f-87a4-514d078fdaaf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b7feb475-a410-4d2f-87a4-514d078fdaaf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c8f3-0f7b-70a2-b5d7-011fe6eee7ea"},"task_id":"01a0c8f3-0f7b-70a2-b5d7-011fe6eee7ea","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c8f3-0f7b-70a2-b5d7-011fe6eee7ea","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-82-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -40 LOGBOOK.md; echo ===; grep -n -i \\\"deadline\\\\|generation\\\\|attach\\\" README.md | head -20\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook format and README claims\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev6 — attach/quiesce ordering contract; closure-authority escalation\\n\\n- P1-B FIXED: attach now revalidates the quiesce barrier under `Lifecycle.barrierMu` immediately before committing its writable client receipt, holding the lock through the receipt, the returned vector, and the advisory memory record; quiesce holds the same lock across engine closure plus report commit, boundary across its report commit only (the wait blocks on the wrapper signal). Contract: report commits and receipt commits are mutually exclusive, whichever lands first wins, no writable receipt commits after a durable closure report. Three committed tests: paused-admission late attach refuses, plus quiesce/boundary overlap tests that launch attach from inside the report write via the state crash seam and assert it blocks then refuses. Narrowings `N-attach-barrier-recheck` and `N-ordering-lock-{attach,quiesce,boundary}` (instance-scoped) all KILLED; symmetry attach 1 / quiesce 1 / boundary 1.\\n- P1-A ESCALATED (structural, not a fourth guard): a lost outcome-report write after committed engine closure still admits a fresh writable attach until retry heals the report, because admission consults the outcome proof alone and pending-vs-committed is unrepresentable there. Bound B43 names owner `internal/terminstance ReceiptStore` and the scoped contract (completed-closure enumeration distinguishing pending-without-completion from completed); row 79 now claims only the lost state-record write fails closed. Same window covers receipt/report crash and double loss. B42 states the in-process bound on the ordering lock (cross-process needs a lock file) and that the covered vector handoff ends at construction.\\n- P2-A CLOSED: three read-error arms now fail closed through `Execute(attach)` with tests plus reviewer-shaped narrowings — incarnation EISDIR-as-absence (`N-incarnation-read-absent`), outcomes ENOTDIR-as-absence (`N-outcomes-dir-read-absent`), outcome-file EISDIR skip via `.json`-symlink-to-dir (`N-outcome-file-read-skip`) — and the attach entry of the unsafe-root gate carries its own valid-body test plus `N-attach-entry-root-custody` (weakened attach is served, proving admission rather than rerouting).\\n- P2-B CLOSED: importer outcome corpus now covers 36/36 packages (198 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 7 declared candidate-only; 6/6 stable runs) with `cloneproject.Normalize` no-fetcher/no-sink refusals, `sshtransport.New(zero)` invalid-snapshot refusal, and `crashgate.Lookup` known/unknown rows. Suite-verdict grid: 23,874 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 505 candidate-only additions, 0 fails.\\n- P3 CLOSED: Table C recounted from the Table D gate set (140 gates × 11 = 1540; total census 255 measured of 5248 with 186 bounds and 4807 unreachable, verified by script); row 72 lease-members prose corrected to the ownership-neutral authorization; README quiesce claim narrowed to report-committed refusal plus B43; battery counts updated (281 tmuxserver rows: 277 narrowing + 3 supplementary + control).\\n- PROCESS: an overlap test that consumes the attach result inside the hook then re-waits on the same channel hangs 10s under the lock-removal plant; putting the result back keeps the kill fast with two failure lines. Copying the outcome-grid driver into a tree breaks `go test ./...` via the specdoc no-product-command gate — run the driver, remove the directory, then run the suite.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### BUG-260917-3lddu0 — superseded leases are refused before append admission\\n\\n- FIX: `Repository.AppendEvent` now calls `checkWinningLease` after loading the durable lease winner and before `checkAppend`. Lower-epoch events refuse `ErrStaleLease`; same-epoch losing leases refuse `ErrDivergentBranch`. Refused branch bytes remain immutable and addressable, while the authoritative chain is unchanged. Historical replay intentionally does not apply this owner-side gate.\\n- REPRO: the exact trunk baseline at `799c338e401fca0b24859c0b870cd665927209f2` was driven through an adapted production `AppendEvent` probe: a successor won while the tail still named A, then A's append returned `err=<nil>` and the negative expected stale refusal. The archived review probe 15 records the old blast radius verbatim: losing-lease `profile.changed` drove `profile=yolo` with mapping `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`. The candidate test `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored` now refuses the append and proves `Run` cannot use that source.\\n- AC: 2 of 2 leaf rows are driven. The gate × production-entry census is 8 of 10 cells: 4 lower-epoch and 4 same-epoch loser cells across `AppendEvent`, `SetProfile`, `Emit`, and `EmitParked`; both `Run → EmitParked` cells are bounded as unreachable except by an interleaving between `Observe` and `AppendEvent`, closed by the durable gate. Row symmetry is 4/4 versus 4/4. `N-stale-winning-admission` and `N-same-epoch-winning-admission` retain the gate, admit one reachable rejected class each, and are KILLED twice; controls are classified separately.\\n- LANDED-TEST MEANING TABLE: the name-keyed outcome grid cannot expose four stable-name input changes. `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes`, `TestRunSupersededPairIdenticalRetry`, and `TestRunCreateFromStoppedPostWindow` now publish `session.idle` + `session.stopped` under A before successor B; the old successor-first fixture would move those A-after-B stop events to literal `ErrStaleLease`. `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored` changed from admitting lower-epoch `profile.changed` and checking downstream Run into asserting raw `AppendEvent` refusal; its before outcome was yolo with `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`. The full table and §5.2/§5.3 or §2.4 citations are in the task results and axpane TRACEABILITY.\\n\\n| Stable-name test | Moved input / meaning | Spec |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes`; `TestRunSupersededPairIdenticalRetry`; `TestRunCreateFromStoppedPostWindow` | A-owned `session.idle` + `session.stopped` after B would now be `ErrStaleLease`; each fixture now publishes before B. | §5.2/§5.3 |\\n| `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored` | A-owned lower-epoch `profile.changed` after B was admitted/yolo before; now raw `AppendEvent` refuses and preserves it, so profile stays standard/no source. | §2.4 + §5.3 |\\n- IMPORTER DIFF: complete importer mask is `./internal/axpane ./internal/crashgate ./internal/fencing ./internal/sessckpt ./internal/sessprofile ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessstate ./internal/termbind ./internal/terminstance`. The old comparison is a test-status grid: 2,018/2,030 keys including 9 package rows, or 2,009/2,021 actual test rows; 12 named additions, 0 removed, 0 changed statuses; all 9 package summaries PASS. It is not runtime admission evidence. The adopted reviewer runtime grid over the same nine-package importer set records 130 outcome keys / 2,926 calls before versus 137 / 2,955 after, with 10 added and 3 removed outcome keys; every moved arm is named in the results and matrix. Direct sessrepo tests are outside the importer mask and named in the matrix.\\n- TRACEABILITY: route (b) owns the losing-profile registry case at `internal/sessrepo/sessrepo.go:AppendEvent`; independent lease-aware derivation-side authority is a bound owned by `STORY-260922-cpkajd` / `TASK-260922-31qyyi`, not an independent guarantee in this leaf. The case is referenced by Section 2.4 clause 2.4#2. Candidate registry digest is re-derived after that edge as `174728a8a01e8429004e4f9c4687f8fa1f17406b641012236c3427a758baf31e`; exact-tree tracecheck prints `contracts=64 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=154 fixtures=33 compatibility_contracts=55 assigned_scopes=0` and `section coverage: bindings=69 full=4 partial=9 sliver=9 unevidenced=43 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=70/574`. Section 2.4 admits; section 5.3 correctly refuses assigned-scope admission at 7/8 partial coverage.\\n- P3 DISPOSITIONS: the axpane `decide.go` “lapsed grants refuse” qualifier remains untouched and is scoped to the local-owner path; `observeRemoteWinner` structural redundancy is record-only; the grant-less remote interactive-owner step-4 product question remains unresolved and undecided; unknown higher epoch and empty lease-store behavior are named bounds with owners; evidence records the final candidate TREE OID in the task matrix and keeps the exact test masks beside every row count.\\n- MUTATION: the shipped harness ran twice under `mutants-append-rev3-pass1/` and `mutants-append-rev3-pass2/`. Both true reachable narrowings are KILLED twice; comment controls SURVIVE, missing-token controls are NOT_APPLIED, syntax controls are COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE, and control-before/after suites exit 0. Raw per-plant logs and exits are retained in both directories.\\n- VALIDATION: the fresh configured run is recorded under `.temp/BUG-260917-3lddu0/validation-rev3/`; all 30 configured commands exited 0. `task-board validate` reported 179 existing `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics and exited 0; scoped tracecheck §2.4 exited 0 and §5.3 exited 1 as the expected 7/8 refusal.\\n- HANDOFF: importer outcomes and tracecheck logs are task-scoped; the candidate remains UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for snapshot handoff.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz — tmux lifecycle operations via structured commands (initial producer delivery)\\n\\n===\\n418:current trust generation and the live local authorization boundary. Trust\\n434:the trust generation in one crash-durable joint commit; `RollbackV4` requires\\n436:assurance and also bumps the generation. Direct `Migrate`/`MigrateOS` calls\\n506:transport, deadlines, size limits, stdout/stderr separation, operation\\n509:`request_id`, `operation`, `deadline`, `body`), starts one plugin process\\n510:per operation, enforces the request deadline, and interprets the single\\n511:response frame. Unknown operations, stale deadlines, and unframeable\\n520:retryable bit, details, or authority. A plugin that exceeds its deadline\\n1954:logs and mutation artifacts are attached to `TASK-260830-1r9wrr`; scratch\\n2056:Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are attached to\\n2114:Task validation logs and conformance artifacts are attached to\\n2151:`attach_remote` or `takeover_offer`; a local owner with the same lapsed grant\\n2175:attached to `TASK-260830-3g12yp`; scratch outputs live under\\n2185:before launching, reattaching, offering, parking, or refusing a provider\\n2188:exactly one of `launch`, `reattach`, `attach_remote`, `takeover_offer`,\\n2205:reattach replays the pair's own recorded child, verified locally held foldable\\n2210:reattaches linearizably on the commit race, and sweeps stale pre-commit\\n2213:bound to the host binding, probed build, and current generation, refusing\\n2240:attached to `TAS