\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":3,\\\"text\\\":\\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":4,\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate x entry census is committed as a table in the conformance matrix and mirrored in TRACEABILITY: every production entry that reaches each gate gets a named test plus an admitting narrowing row, or unreachable with a reason, or a stated bound with an owner; every gate implemented on two or more sides carries a row-count symmetry line\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":9,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every rule is driven to its effect by a committed test that passes with NO tmux process anywhere; any real-tmux test is separately gated and is never the only witness for an acceptance row, and the results state which rows have a real-tmux witness in addition to their deterministic one\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":10,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":11,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":13,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":14,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":15,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":21,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Implementation matches AC\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":23,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Tests green\\\"}}]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2880,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 720,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
